## Before you implement anything

This project keeps its architecture, constraints, and past technical decisions
in `./docs`. **Read `docs/README.md` first** — it is the map and tells you which
files to open for the task at hand. Do not reinvent decisions that already exist.

Hard rules that must never be broken live in `docs/02-constraints/invariants.md`.
Decisions already made (with their rationale) live in `docs/03-decisions/`.

If an implementation would force you to violate an invariant or reverse an
accepted ADR: stop and raise it with the user, or propose a new ADR. Do not
quietly work around it.

## How work is delivered

Agentic SDD, via the `engineer` plugin: `/engineer:requirement` → `/engineer:plan`
→ `/engineer:architect` → `/engineer:build` → `/engineer:release stag|prod`.
`/engineer:status` shows where each version stands. Branches: `main` = STAG,
`release` = PROD, `build/vX.Y.Z.T` per version. Commits follow Conventional
Commits (mandatory).

